## Why This Is Asked
Asynchronous order processing with idempotency is common in production; testing must prove duplicates don't create multiple orders and failures route to DLQs with retries, plus end-to-end visibility.

## Key Concepts
- Idempotency keys, exactly-once processing
- Message queues (Kafka), DLQ design
- Retry/backoff strategies, consumer failure modes
- End-to-end tracing and correlation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example test (pseudo)
const request = require('supertest');
const api = require('supertest')('https://api.example.com');
const idKey = 'order-uniq-123';

test('duplicate submissions do not create duplicates', async () => {
  const r1 = await api.post('/orders').set('Idempotency-Key', idKey).send({items:[{sku:'A1',qty:1}]});
  const r2 = await api.post('/orders').set('Idempotency-Key', idKey).send({items:[{sku:'A1',qty:1}]});
  expect(r1.status).toBe(202);
  expect(r2.status).toBe(202);
  // fetch status after processing
});
```

